{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Elohim has gathered up my reproach.</b> That is, that they used to taunt her. <b>And she called his name Joseph, saying, 'YHWH add to me another son'</b> — and in the mention of the name Joseph she hinted at this. And the fact that she said 'another son' and did not say 'other sons' indicates that she knew this through divine inspiration, for Leah already had six sons, and Bilhah and Zilpah two each, making ten; and since Joseph was born, being the eleventh, she knew that there would yet be born to her one more son to complete the twelve." "<b>And behold</b> Rachel mentioned in him two expressions: the expression of gathering and the expression of addition — openly in the expression of addition, and in the hidden in the expression of gathering: אסף אלהים את חרפתי. This is to indicate that Joseph alludes to the middle line, which gathers in all the camps, joining all the extremities above and below. And behold, its branches drawn forth from it are Netsaḥ and Hod; therefore from Joseph there emerged two tribes, Manasseh and Ephraim. And Benjamin corresponded to the two attributes above him. And his mother called him בן אוני — that is, 'son of my strength,' which is the attribute of Judgment. And his father called him Benjamin, which is Mercy — that is, 'son of the right hand.' And two other attributes I have already hinted at in Dan and Naphtali. And understand that Dan and Naphtali are Ẓedek and Ẓadik, and Joseph is the middle line with its branches, and Benjamin is ידי אביר יעקב — the hands of the mighty one of Jacob — receiving from above him; if so, all is included in all, and this is clear."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:34.010480828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}